{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\windows\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command \"rg -n \\\"run state|RunState|orchestration state|durable local\\\" doc tests .agentic-sdlc contracts-import -g '*.md' -g '*.py'\"","aggregated_output":"contracts-import\\260906\\P1-C03_RUNTIME_COMPOSITION.md:78:Title: Persist RunResearchRuntime orchestration state durably\ncontracts-import\\260906\\P1-C03_RUNTIME_COMPOSITION.md:81:The Product Composition Layer MUST provide a durable local store for the existing RunResearchRuntime `state_store` seam so run-level orchestration state can be reloaded after rebuilding a RunScope. The store MUST be keyed by AgentRun, use local durable storage, and write atomically.\ncontracts-import\\260906\\P1-C03_RUNTIME_COMPOSITION.md:87:Title: Preserve durable checkpoint ordering between SQL state and run state\ncontracts-import\\260906\\P1-C03_RUNTIME_COMPOSITION.md:165:Saving run-orchestration state MUST create or replace one AgentRun-keyed durable local state representation atomically, and loading it from a newly created store instance MUST reproduce the saved RunResearchRuntime state needed by the existing runtime seam.\ncontracts-import\\260906\\P1-C03_RUNTIME_COMPOSITION.md:174:After rebuilding RuntimeFactory/RunScope in a fresh process-equivalent test context, the new RunScope MUST be able to read the previously persisted run-level orchestration state for the same AgentRun.\ncontracts-import\\260906\\P1-C03_RUNTIME_COMPOSITION.md:226:- Add only the durable local store needed for the existing RunResearchRuntime state-store seam.\ncontracts-import\\260906\\P1-C03_RUNTIME_COMPOSITION.md:233:- Use an AgentRun-scoped local path such as `data/layer3/runs/<agent_run_id>/run_state.json` for run-orchestration state.\ncontracts-import\\260906\\P1-C03_RUNTIME_COMPOSITION.md:268:The new run-orchestration state store MUST use local durable storage and atomic replacement; it MUST NOT require a new database table unless the existing code already makes that strictly necessary for the current runtime seam.\ncontracts-import\\260906\\P1-C03_RUNTIME_COMPOSITION.md:286:Provide an AgentRun-keyed durable local state store compatible with the existing RunResearchRuntime state-store seam, including atomic writes and reload behavior.\ncontracts-import\\260903\\TransitScholar-L3S7-PSC-Contract-v2-approved.md:32:  \"contract_summary\": \"Implement Layer3 Stage7 Memory and Knowledge Evolution. L3S7 adds a non-owning WorkingMemory facade over existing current-run state, Workspace-scoped Episodic Memory distilled once per AgentRun through deterministic collection plus LLM semantic distillation plus deterministic validation, and Workspace-scoped Semantic Memory through KnowledgeCandidate promotion into an entry/page-based Agentic Wiki. Episodic Memory remains auxiliary experience available only through context governance to RunCoordinatorRole and QueryPlanningRole. Agentic Wiki remains provenance-grounded in Claims and Evidence, is maintained independently from Base Wiki, participates in Wiki retrieval with explicit source identity, and performs lightweight provenance maintenance before Session use. Version 2 additionally authorizes the final acceptance task to update obsolete L3S1 regression guards that categorically prohibit AgenticWiki symbols in Layer3, while preserving all L3S1 Workspace isolation, lifecycle, and global Paper/L2S1 ownership semantics.\"\ncontracts-import\\260903\\TransitScholar-L3S7-PSC-Contract-v2-approved.md:64:L3S7 MUST provide a WorkingMemory facade or equivalent unified access boundary over already existing current-run state and context, including relevant ResearchState, Query/Evidence/Claim Ledger state, RoleWorkingState, RunOrchestrationState, Runtime/Run context snapshots, and Session handoff state.\ncontracts-import\\260903\\TransitScholar-L3S7-PSC-Contract-v2-approved.md:203:L3S7 MUST derive useful_queries and failed_or_unhelpful_queries from authoritative Query/Evidence/run state rather than from LLM recollection.\ncontracts-import\\260903\\TransitScholar-L3S7-PSC-Contract-v2-approved.md:738:A Claim that was proposed earlier in a run but is rejected by the durable end-of-run state is not eligible for the run-end candidate source pool.\ncontracts-import\\260903\\TransitScholar-L3S7-PSC-Contract-v2-approved.md:954:  - Working Memory = current-run state already owned by L3S2-L3S6;\ncontracts-import\\260903\\TransitScholar-L3S7-PSC-Contract-v2-approved.md:977:- Derive useful_queries and failed_or_unhelpful_queries from durable Query/Evidence/run state.\ncontracts-import\\260903\\TransitScholar-L3S7-PSC-Contract-v2-approved.md:1048:  - run state;\ncontracts-import\\260903\\TransitScholar-L3S7-PSC-Contract-v2-approved.md:1268:Define the three L3S7 memory semantics and implement a non-owning WorkingMemory access facade over existing current-run state without duplicating authoritative persistence.\ncontracts-import\\260906\\P1-C04_PRODUCT_CLOSURE.md:81:The product layer MUST expose a read-only `ProductRunState` projection derived from existing Core authoritative state and a conversation view that combines ConversationTurn display data with the associated derived run state. The projection MUST NOT be persisted as a new source of truth and MUST NOT gain write authority over AgentRun, ResearchSession, RoleExecution, ledger, memory, wiki, or trace state.\ncontracts-import\\260906\\P1-C04_PRODUCT_CLOSURE.md:166:`ProductRunState` MUST be derivable from existing AgentRun, run orchestration, ResearchSession/ResearchState, RoleExecution, and/or trace data and MUST NOT require a persisted ProductRunState table/file.\ncontracts-import\\260906\\P1-C04_PRODUCT_CLOSURE.md:182:A conversation view MUST expose ordered turn display data, including user message, resolved user goal, persisted assistant response, linked AgentRun identifier, and associated derived run state when available, without mutating 